  "description": "PECFEJ crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I -4 c 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H122 O42 Sm9 1+,C10 H1 Mo2 O10 1-. From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2E (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2B (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2G (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm3E (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm3G (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm3B (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Mo1 (Mo) has 0 O neighbors; Mo1M (Mo) has 0 O neighbors; Sm4? (Sm) has 0 O neighbors; Sm5? (Sm) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.690-5.258 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.88-169.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Sm9(acac)16(OH)10][Mo2(CO)10(μ-H)]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 10 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 10 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
